STEP 9 · VISUAL CHECK
  Run. Playwright chromium present, tool-call budget well under the ceiling, entry
  has images. 2 captures, 2 corrective edits, 1 re-capture. Under every cap.

  BREAKAGE FOUND (same root cause on both pages):
    `.hero > *{position:relative}` and `.viewer > *{position:relative}` were each
    written after the `.lamp{position:absolute}` rule at equal specificity (0,1,0),
    so the later rule won and the lamp div reverted to static flow. The lamp then
    claimed its own height as layout: 780px of dead space above the landing hero,
    420px above the demo's frame viewer. Both pages opened on a blank screen.
  FIX: raised the lamp selectors to `.hero > .lamp` and `.viewer > .lamp` (0,2,0),
  which now beat the container rule. Landing full-page height fell from 4787px to
  4007px and the lamp reads as intended, a soft pool behind the headline.
  Re-capture confirms the hero, telemetry wells and both CTAs sit above the fold.

  NOT FIXED, deliberately: below-fold sections render blank in the full-page
  capture because `.rise` starts at opacity 0 and the IntersectionObserver never
  fires in a screenshot that does not scroll. Verified this is a capture artifact
  rather than a page defect. Left alone under the "fix only real breakage" rule.
  Demo capture reviewed and clean: reticle-framed dossier portrait, subject rail
  with scores and class tags, telemetry wells, citation chain and the contested
  rail with working flag toggles all land correctly.

